    "result_text": "All tests pass (3/3, BUILD SUCCESS). Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nAn owner may now include an optional 4-digit `postcode`, validated only when present, stored, and returned.\n\n**Validation rule** (in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `validatePostcode`):\n- Absent/blank postcode \u2192 accepted (contract stays backward-compatible).\n- Present \u2192 must be exactly 4 digits, else **400**.\n- When the city has a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), the postcode must fall in that region's inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), else **400**.\n- A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry it and it round-trips in requests/responses.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `postcode` column + getter/setter (MapStruct auto-maps it both directions).\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `postcode` column (hsqldb is what the tests run against; the others for parity).\n- **`rest/advice/InvalidPostcodeException.java`** (new) + a handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** returning **400** with `errors: [\"postcode\"]`, mirroring the existing telephone/email exception pattern.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the `validatePostcode`/`region` helpers and the validation call in `addOwner`.\n\nOne bug caught during testing: `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE for unknown-region cities (immutable maps reject null keys), so I guard the region lookup before the map access.\n\nI scoped this to the create path (`POST /api/owners`), which is what the spec describes (\"an owner *created* without a postcode is still accepted\") and what the acceptance tests exercise; `updateOwner` was left untouched, so an existing owner's stored postcode is preserved across updates.",
